# Trivy ignore file - vulnerabilities reviewed and explicitly accepted.
# Applies to the `docker` Maven profile scans (trivy-html-report + trivy-gate).
#
# Add one CVE ID per line. For each entry, keep a comment block above it that
# records:
#   - the affected artifact(s) and version(s),
#   - why no upstream fix is available (or why upgrading is blocked),
#   - the risk assessment for this project.
#
# The gate already runs with --ignore-unfixed, so entries here are only needed
# for HIGH/CRITICAL findings that DO have a fix but we consciously choose not
# to take (e.g. transitive from a locked BOM, or breaking change).
